Note that Example 08 demonstrates the Eathon module system and true stack frame recursion across both ELF64 and C99 backends.

Include module mathlib.

Display Eathon Modules and Native Recursion Suite.

Call absVal with neg 42 into positiveFortyTwo.
Display Absolute value of neg 42, positiveFortyTwo.

Call clampVal with 180, 0, 100 into clampedPercent.
Display Clamped percentage, clampedPercent.

Call power with 3, 5 into threeToFifth.
Display Three to the fifth power, threeToFifth.

Call factorial with 6 into factSix.
Display Factorial of 6, factSix.
